1
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:08,942
Michiko! This way! Look at all the people!

2
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:12,345
That's so far! Hold on!

3
00:00:12,445 --> 00:00:15,849
You sure eat a lot, Michiko.
What, you want this?

4
00:00:15,949 --> 00:00:19,552
Kaminari-okoshi <i>and</i> ningyo-yaki.
<i>Oh, that's hot!</i>

5
00:00:19,619 --> 00:00:23,757
<i>You sure ate a lot. Even that!
One, two, three, four, five...</i>

6
00:00:23,823 --> 00:00:25,925
I could still eat a ton!

7
00:00:25,992 --> 00:00:27,827
- What?
- Let's end with <i>monja.</i>

8
00:00:27,927 --> 00:00:29,596
- What? You want more?
- Why not?

9
00:00:29,662 --> 00:00:31,931
- You will get fat!
- Akira, isn't that amazing?

10
00:00:31,998 --> 00:00:34,200
- What a performance!
- Let's have a look!

11
00:00:35,435 --> 00:00:37,704
- Get a photo!
- Let's get photos!

12
00:00:37,804 --> 00:00:40,407
They're totally in unison!

13
00:00:40,507 --> 00:00:41,908
That's so cool!

14
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:47,147
AKIRA KANBARA, MANAGER
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

15
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:48,782
That was amazing, Akira!

16
00:00:51,951 --> 00:00:53,420
That was magnificent!

17
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:56,489
You'll take a picture?

18
00:00:57,424 --> 00:00:58,825
Ready!

19
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:04,864
Thank you!

20
00:01:05,665 --> 00:01:07,901
One thousand yen, please.

21
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:09,135
One thousand yen?

22
00:01:12,705 --> 00:01:15,842
- One thousand yen.
- Are you kidding me?

23
00:01:15,942 --> 00:01:18,111
- Fine. I'll pay.
- You're paying?

24
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:19,746
- Give me back my phone.
- Give it back.

25
00:01:19,846 --> 00:01:22,749
- Unbelievable!
- That's awful! Can you believe it?

26
00:01:22,849 --> 00:01:25,518
- What a total rip-off.
- One thousand yen, please.

27
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:28,221
- One thousand yen, please.
- What? Again?

28
00:01:28,354 --> 00:01:31,624
- No way! I don't have any money!
- One thousand yen, please.

29
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:32,892
One thousand yen, please.

30
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:36,629
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

31
00:01:38,465 --> 00:01:42,802
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

32
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:48,274
<i>Hospital Director Hiruma will now
make a round of visits.</i>

33
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:52,979
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

34
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:55,048
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

35
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:57,951
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

36
00:01:58,017 --> 00:02:00,086
Director Hiruma!

37
00:02:00,153 --> 00:02:02,722
Congratulations on starting
the director's rounds again.

38
00:02:02,822 --> 00:02:04,524
It's only natural, after all.

39
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:06,759
- Don't break ranks.
- Right. Sorry.

40
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:11,998
- It's a Japanese doctor parade.
- It's a Japanese doctor parade.

41
00:02:16,870 --> 00:02:18,972
This is so embarrassing. Please stop this.

42
00:02:19,038 --> 00:02:21,841
The director's rounds were abolished.

43
00:02:22,075 --> 00:02:24,878
But I am the hospital director.

44
00:02:24,944 --> 00:02:28,581
You all love doing
the director's rounds, right?

45
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:29,983
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

46
00:02:30,049 --> 00:02:32,452
Out of the way. Make way.

47
00:02:32,785 --> 00:02:35,121
Good. Thank you.

48
00:02:36,623 --> 00:02:38,725
Japanese fish are too weak.

49
00:02:38,791 --> 00:02:42,162
At this rate, they'll be gobbled up
by invasive species.

50
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:45,532
That's what I told you
when we first met, right?

51
00:02:46,399 --> 00:02:50,603
That's why I eat the invasive black bass,

52
00:02:50,904 --> 00:02:53,273
to protect the weak Japanese fish.

53
00:02:54,073 --> 00:02:57,010
But those weak Japanese fish
want their director's rounds

54
00:02:57,110 --> 00:02:59,145
and never cut the important things.

55
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:01,181
It's all so wasteful!

56
00:03:02,749 --> 00:03:06,319
The crisis has only increased after
I attended the Paris conference.

57
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:09,556
Japanese medicine should be
at the forefront of medicine,

58
00:03:09,622 --> 00:03:11,691
but it continues to fall behind the world.

59
00:03:11,991 --> 00:03:14,327
What's worse,
the head of this university hospital

60
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:16,229
won't even face this reality!

61
00:03:16,296 --> 00:03:19,165
He's cute. Who is that? A love child?

62
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,634
Dr. Daimon,

63
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:24,704
with your brilliant skills,

64
00:03:25,638 --> 00:03:27,740
use this Totei University Hospital

65
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:30,009
to save Japanese medicine!

66
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:34,480
If we work together,
nothing is impossible.

67
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,322
Was it to your liking?

68
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,556
Yes, it was delicious.

69
00:03:43,623 --> 00:03:46,292
Thank you for the delicious meal.

70
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:47,360
You're welcome.

71
00:03:47,927 --> 00:03:50,597
- You'll help me, won't you?
- I decline.

72
00:03:52,365 --> 00:03:54,000
The free lunch was a big help.

73
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:55,501
- Thanks.
- Wait.

74
00:03:56,703 --> 00:03:58,871
Dr. Daimon, there's a patient

75
00:03:59,038 --> 00:04:01,207
I want you to perform a transplant for.

76
00:04:01,274 --> 00:04:04,744
Why didn't you tell me sooner?
Okay, Nichotan!

77
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:07,747
- How many patients? Ten? One hundred?
- One.

78
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:10,917
He is essential
if we are to rescue this hospital.

79
00:04:11,284 --> 00:04:14,087
Just one? Okay, what part do I operate on?

80
00:04:16,322 --> 00:04:19,025
- A brain transplant?
- No.

81
00:04:19,492 --> 00:04:21,027
A hair graft.

82
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,763
That is to say, the most advanced

83
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:26,933
hair replacement.

84
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:28,968
Hair?

85
00:04:31,070 --> 00:04:32,038
Tange!

86
00:04:51,324 --> 00:04:55,561
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor,
who was never part of</i>

87
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:59,232
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

88
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:04,971
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

89
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:08,708
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

90
00:05:08,841 --> 00:05:11,911
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

91
00:05:12,011 --> 00:05:13,379
<i>are her weapons.</i>

92
00:05:14,681 --> 00:05:16,883
"I'm surprised the master surgeon
is a Japanese beauty.

93
00:05:17,784 --> 00:05:20,720
Japanese women are devoted
to serving men, right?

94
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,923
Walk three steps behind me.

95
00:05:24,123 --> 00:05:26,025
Kindly serve me."

96
00:05:26,292 --> 00:05:27,260
I decline.

97
00:05:28,528 --> 00:05:29,629
I don't need a translator.

98
00:05:35,468 --> 00:05:37,070
Dr. Daimon, watch your mouth.

99
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:05,064
Seven!

100
00:06:09,802 --> 00:06:10,903
Seven!

101
00:06:13,072 --> 00:06:14,140
Seven!

102
00:06:17,744 --> 00:06:19,979
Tenderness in epigastric region.

103
00:06:20,179 --> 00:06:22,415
- Emergency endoscope! Stretcher!
- Right!

104
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:36,763
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

105
00:06:36,963 --> 00:06:39,966
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

106
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:16,369
Please operate immediately.

107
00:07:19,038 --> 00:07:19,872
Seven!

108
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,385
For today's pre-op conference,

109
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:35,188
Director Ushio is away
at an international conference.

110
00:07:35,888 --> 00:07:37,723
Now, for the first patient.

111
00:07:38,691 --> 00:07:43,229
CEO of Goldberg Bank, Seven Goldberg.

112
00:07:43,663 --> 00:07:45,965
Stomach cancer, stage 1B.

113
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:49,435
There is a four-centimeter tumor
on the stomach's lesser curvature.

114
00:07:49,669 --> 00:07:53,706
It has penetrated the submucosa
and metastasized to the lymph nodes.

115
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:58,344
Say, Daimon, I may not look it,
but my English is pretty good.

116
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:01,347
In high school, I went to
summer school there every summer.

117
00:08:01,447 --> 00:08:03,616
Quit the chatter during meetings.

118
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:09,322
Assistant Director,
as for treatment for the Goldberg CEO--

119
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:11,691
- I'll do the operation!
- Assistant Director!

120
00:08:11,757 --> 00:08:14,327
Let me be the CEO's attending physician.

121
00:08:14,393 --> 00:08:15,561
No.

122
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:20,299
The CEO requires a total gastrectomy.

123
00:08:20,766 --> 00:08:22,668
The Roux-en-Y procedure is
best for reconstruction.

124
00:08:22,735 --> 00:08:24,504
The Roux-en-Y procedure?

125
00:08:24,604 --> 00:08:27,206
How many millennia ago is
that procedure from?

126
00:08:27,306 --> 00:08:30,409
How can you operate on
stomach cancer in this day and age?

127
00:08:30,610 --> 00:08:32,311
You're a useless relic.

128
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:34,914
"A useless relic"? How rude!

129
00:08:35,114 --> 00:08:36,949
The most advanced treatment is

130
00:08:37,049 --> 00:08:39,852
molecular target drugs
and immunity building drugs.

131
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,788
There is less burden on the patient,

132
00:08:42,889 --> 00:08:45,358
and treatment can be administered
out-of-hospital.

133
00:08:45,491 --> 00:08:48,127
Can he return to his country
in three weeks?

134
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:51,964
- That's not possible--
- I can do it in a week!

135
00:08:52,632 --> 00:08:54,967
- Let me operate.
- Dr. Daimon!

136
00:08:55,801 --> 00:08:58,404
Have you already forgotten
how rudely you spoke to him?

137
00:08:58,838 --> 00:09:01,474
- What did I say?
- CEO Goldberg was

138
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:04,510
deeply offended by your rude comments.

139
00:09:04,844 --> 00:09:06,412
He says he doesn't want to see you.

140
00:09:06,579 --> 00:09:09,382
Daimon, you've been banned.

141
00:09:09,916 --> 00:09:10,883
No way.

142
00:09:12,285 --> 00:09:14,987
If the total gastrectomy is
performed using

143
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:16,689
the laparoscope, my specialty,

144
00:09:16,789 --> 00:09:18,691
he can return to his country in two weeks.

145
00:09:18,758 --> 00:09:19,926
Is that right?

146
00:09:20,626 --> 00:09:23,429
Then I'd like you to do it, Dr. Kaji.

147
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:24,397
Yes, sir!

148
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:28,000
Director Kaji, I can be your assistant!

149
00:09:30,836 --> 00:09:34,540
My first assistant will be Dr. Hara.

150
00:09:36,142 --> 00:09:38,344
My second assistant will be

151
00:09:39,011 --> 00:09:40,546
Tako. If you would, please.

152
00:09:40,613 --> 00:09:42,181
- Yes.
- Yes!

153
00:09:42,715 --> 00:09:46,185
Dr. Kaji, can you speak English?
I can translate if--

154
00:09:46,319 --> 00:09:48,988
- I don't need it! How rude!
- Dr. Kaji...

155
00:09:49,055 --> 00:09:52,625
Dr. Kaji reads medical articles
in English!

156
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,561
- Then I'm sorry.
- You better be.

157
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:58,931
Dr. Hara, you worked in
a Russian hospital,

158
00:09:58,998 --> 00:10:01,467
- so language isn't an issue, right?
- That's right.

159
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:06,072
- Please take care of it, everyone.
- Yes, sir!

160
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,575
And he was my patient.

161
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:14,380
Why the heck does everyone
treat me like a pariah?

162
00:10:15,748 --> 00:10:20,953
Anyone who treats me like a pariah
will suffer for it later.

163
00:10:21,354 --> 00:10:23,022
Just you wait and see.

164
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,525
- Say, Ruri.
- Yes?

165
00:10:27,393 --> 00:10:30,196
What do you think of me, Ruri?

166
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,836
I knew you were always on my side.

167
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:48,280
I'm Director Kaji of Next-Generation
Ultra-Minimally Invasive Surgery.

168
00:10:58,591 --> 00:10:59,692
I'm Tako.

169
00:11:00,459 --> 00:11:04,630
Anyway, enough introductions.
Let's begin the screening.

170
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:13,739
I see you understand Japanese, Natalie.

171
00:11:13,873 --> 00:11:18,811
Yes. I love Japanese anime,
so I've studied a little.

172
00:11:18,878 --> 00:11:20,146
Magnificent.

173
00:11:28,487 --> 00:11:29,588
Seven.

174
00:12:18,104 --> 00:12:20,339
When I asked,
"You don't have any allergies, do you?"

175
00:12:20,439 --> 00:12:21,841
he answered, "Yes," right?

176
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:24,210
Let's confirm it again.

177
00:12:35,454 --> 00:12:36,322
Is that all?

178
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,530
GENERAL SURGERY DEPARTMENT

179
00:12:46,232 --> 00:12:49,335
Dang, Director Kaji and Dr. Hara,
you're amazing.

180
00:12:49,401 --> 00:12:52,071
I can't believe you understood
his fast English.

181
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:54,740
It's a good thing Dr. Kaji was there.

182
00:12:54,907 --> 00:12:56,675
I didn't want to ask him over and over.

183
00:12:56,742 --> 00:12:58,210
I was going to ask Dr. Kaji later.

184
00:12:58,277 --> 00:12:59,879
Are you serious?

185
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,214
You didn't understand him?

186
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:05,117
My Russian is perfect,
but I'm bad at English.

187
00:13:05,317 --> 00:13:06,519
You're kidding me!

188
00:13:07,319 --> 00:13:09,789
If you didn't understand,
you can't expect me to!

189
00:13:09,855 --> 00:13:10,890
Are you serious?

190
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,159
But you always read articles in English.

191
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,529
I can read,

192
00:13:17,163 --> 00:13:19,698
- but my listening is non-existent.
- Really?

193
00:13:19,765 --> 00:13:21,700
Neither of you understood him?

194
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:23,702
- I thought you understood!
- What do we do?

195
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:24,837
What do we do now?

196
00:13:24,904 --> 00:13:26,639
Let's screen him again with a translator.

197
00:13:26,772 --> 00:13:30,142
No way! Mr. Goldberg was really upset.

198
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:33,712
If we do the screening again,
I'll be taken off his case.

199
00:13:33,779 --> 00:13:34,780
Is that right?

200
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,683
- What do we do?
- I thought you understood!

201
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:41,187
- Dr. Hara, we got everything, right?
- Yes.

202
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,822
- We'll operate as planned next week.
- Yes.

203
00:13:42,922 --> 00:13:44,223
- Total gastrectomy.
- Yes, sir.

204
00:13:44,356 --> 00:13:47,526
Really? Total? You want me to do it?

205
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,562
That's unnecessary! How rude!

206
00:13:52,231 --> 00:13:54,266
Are you making fun of me? How dare you!

207
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:57,570
How dare you talk to me in English!

208
00:13:57,636 --> 00:14:01,674
- How dare you say that!
- Dr. Kaji, calm down!

209
00:14:03,242 --> 00:14:06,879
You know that's the kind of
attitude she has.

210
00:14:07,546 --> 00:14:09,849
What have I done?

211
00:14:09,949 --> 00:14:13,152
I've had so much stress since
becoming director. I'm so irritable!

212
00:14:13,285 --> 00:14:14,520
- Is this menopause?
- No.

213
00:14:14,587 --> 00:14:17,590
Who cares about that?
What about Mr. Goldberg's screening?

214
00:14:20,159 --> 00:14:21,927
- Director!
- Dr. Kaji!

215
00:14:21,994 --> 00:14:24,263
- Are you okay?
- Let's go over there for a second.

216
00:14:24,563 --> 00:14:27,266
- No! Wait!
- Let's go over here for a second.

217
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:30,302
- What do we do?
- I have to go and operate.

218
00:14:30,402 --> 00:14:32,972
- This is bad.
- I'm going to operating room two.

219
00:14:33,072 --> 00:14:35,074
- Bye!
- Wait! This is big trouble!

220
00:14:35,341 --> 00:14:37,843
- This is big trouble! Come on!
- I'm feeling sick!

221
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,378
Hey, wait!

222
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,781
- Tako.
- Yes?

223
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,450
Everyone is so lively.

224
00:14:46,118 --> 00:14:48,320
- This is bad.
- Yes, it's really bad.

225
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:51,757
Since I became a plebe,
my pay was cut by more than half.

226
00:14:52,324 --> 00:14:55,728
It pains my wife that we can't pay
for my child's cram school.

227
00:14:56,595 --> 00:14:59,031
And I have a little secret.

228
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:01,367
- I started part-time work.
- Part-time work?

229
00:15:01,433 --> 00:15:02,401
With a foreign company.

230
00:15:02,468 --> 00:15:05,604
I can use my English,
so I think I'm suited to it.

231
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,907
A foreign clinic?

232
00:15:12,444 --> 00:15:16,282
- It's tough physical work though.
- Yes, but this is big trouble!

233
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:27,459
<i>We wasted money in Asakusa,
so money is tight this month.</i>

234
00:15:27,526 --> 00:15:29,395
I know.

235
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:40,439
We got ripped off for 2,000 yen.

236
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,075
Kabuki? Awesome!

237
00:15:44,843 --> 00:15:50,582
I love Japanese Kabuki,
anime, and cosplay.

238
00:15:51,083 --> 00:15:52,451
Is that so?

239
00:15:52,718 --> 00:15:55,587
- Is this Asakusa?
- Yes. Kaminarimon.

240
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:57,356
I want to go there!

241
00:15:58,190 --> 00:16:00,359
- Take me.
- No way.

242
00:16:02,027 --> 00:16:03,996
I want to pray to the Kannon in Asakusa

243
00:16:04,063 --> 00:16:06,632
for Seven's surgery to be a success.

244
00:16:07,032 --> 00:16:11,003
Please. And I want my photo taken
with these people.

245
00:16:11,070 --> 00:16:13,839
- Please!
- No way!

246
00:16:13,906 --> 00:16:16,008
Where are those guys?

247
00:16:16,575 --> 00:16:18,243
I wonder where they are.

248
00:16:18,944 --> 00:16:20,779
There they are!

249
00:16:21,914 --> 00:16:25,551
- I'm sorry to make you join me.
- Take good care of her.

250
00:16:25,784 --> 00:16:30,522
The wife of Goldberg Bank's CEO?
That's fantastic.

251
00:16:30,622 --> 00:16:33,726
- Yes, maybe... Wait! Oh, no!
- Oh, no!

252
00:16:35,861 --> 00:16:37,730
How totally cool!

253
00:16:41,266 --> 00:16:43,002
How cool!

254
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:46,005
Let's take a photo together.

255
00:16:46,071 --> 00:16:49,408
- They'll rip you off!
- Cheese!

256
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:51,276
What a waste again.

257
00:16:58,050 --> 00:16:58,917
Five thousand yen.

258
00:16:59,885 --> 00:17:02,788
- I've heard this voice before.
- Yes, you're right.

259
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,890
Hold on!

260
00:17:05,991 --> 00:17:08,460
- Dr. Ebina!
- You spotted me.

261
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,396
- Daimon.
- What are you doing?

262
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:12,197
- Part-time job.
- Part-time?

263
00:17:12,264 --> 00:17:14,466
Say, is my face frightening?

264
00:17:15,467 --> 00:17:18,771
- Less frightening than usual.
- That's so mean!

265
00:17:22,007 --> 00:17:24,643
Action picture, 10,000 yen.

266
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:26,045
Discount, 6,000 yen, okay?

267
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,314
Here goes!

268
00:17:30,482 --> 00:17:31,917
That's so cool!

269
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,755
- He's actually pretty good.
- Yes.

270
00:17:41,026 --> 00:17:41,994
OKONOMIYAKI

271
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:44,997
Things must be tough for Dr. Ebina too.

272
00:17:45,130 --> 00:17:48,467
When he became an ordinary
medical staff, his salary was cut.

273
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:51,437
That must hurt
swinging his head around like that.

274
00:17:51,703 --> 00:17:56,475
It's all for money.
Making a living isn't easy.

275
00:17:58,210 --> 00:18:00,646
I never fail.

276
00:18:00,712 --> 00:18:03,082
- How beautiful.
- Here you are.

277
00:18:06,285 --> 00:18:09,088
- Yours is great, Akira!
- I told you so.

278
00:18:09,822 --> 00:18:11,190
Delicious.

279
00:18:11,824 --> 00:18:14,126
I want Seven to have this too.

280
00:18:14,193 --> 00:18:16,795
He loves Japan's B-rank cuisine.

281
00:18:17,463 --> 00:18:20,399
You can actually order take away here.

282
00:18:20,799 --> 00:18:22,701
But isn't he getting stomach surgery?

283
00:18:23,635 --> 00:18:26,438
When he was healthy,
he ate enough for five people.

284
00:18:26,505 --> 00:18:29,341
- By himself? He eats that much?
- Yes.

285
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:33,979
They said it's a total gastrectomy though.

286
00:18:34,179 --> 00:18:36,748
Seven is afraid of surgery.

287
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:39,118
- He's afraid?
- His father died

288
00:18:39,184 --> 00:18:41,386
when he got an appendectomy.

289
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:43,322
An appendectomy?

290
00:18:43,689 --> 00:18:46,925
After the surgery,
he developed a high fever

291
00:18:47,426 --> 00:18:51,196
and went to intensive care,
but they couldn't save him.

292
00:18:51,396 --> 00:18:53,565
That's such a pity.

293
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:58,103
Natalie, eat it before it gets cold.

294
00:18:59,037 --> 00:19:00,305
Okay.

295
00:19:02,274 --> 00:19:05,410
Michiko. Eat up.

296
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:10,482
If it were me, I'd never let him die.

297
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,221
- It's a little cold now.
- It is?

298
00:19:18,624 --> 00:19:20,959
- Nice work, everyone.
- Nice work.

299
00:19:21,059 --> 00:19:22,661
I'll have dinner now.

300
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:27,766
I have to be careful I don't get
a herniated cervical disc doing this.

301
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,801
You're pushing yourself too hard.

302
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:33,071
Being a doctor is easier than this.

303
00:19:33,138 --> 00:19:35,908
- What're you mumbling about?
- Sorry.

304
00:19:35,974 --> 00:19:37,943
- Here's today's pay.
- Thank you!

305
00:19:39,244 --> 00:19:40,779
- There.
- Thank you!

306
00:19:41,313 --> 00:19:43,282
- I hear good things about you.
- Really?

307
00:19:43,382 --> 00:19:44,783
I'll do my best to keep it up.

308
00:19:47,486 --> 00:19:48,954
Excuse me.

309
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:54,593
Oh, no. It's Director Hiruma.

310
00:19:57,563 --> 00:19:59,198
Hello. Ebina speaking.

311
00:19:59,631 --> 00:20:01,400
<i>- Ebina?</i>
- Yes?

312
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,970
<i>I heard you're keeping a secret from me.</i>

313
00:20:05,103 --> 00:20:07,139
<i>You've got a part-time job, don't you?</i>

314
00:20:08,307 --> 00:20:09,408
I'm sorry!

315
00:20:09,474 --> 00:20:11,610
<i>- Get over here right away.</i>
- Yes.

316
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:14,479
Yes, sir! I'll be there immediately!
I'm sorry! Goodbye!

317
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:18,650
Boss, sorry, but I have to go.
Something came up. Can you help me?

318
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,452
Sorry about this. How should I...

319
00:20:24,823 --> 00:20:26,158
FURAIJINMON

320
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:28,894
KAMINARIMON

321
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:36,768
- Excuse me! Sorry I'm late.
- It's okay.

322
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:39,371
- I'm sorry I kept it secret!
- Okay.

323
00:20:41,807 --> 00:20:43,008
- You scared me.
- Sorry.

324
00:20:43,141 --> 00:20:46,278
- What kind of job is it?
- Sorry.

325
00:20:46,345 --> 00:20:48,113
It will take too long to explain.

326
00:20:49,047 --> 00:20:50,949
It's just that I get paid less now,

327
00:20:51,116 --> 00:20:52,751
so if this keeps up,
I can't pay my mortgage.

328
00:20:52,851 --> 00:20:56,355
I don't want to hear it. Cut it out.
Fine. I get it.

329
00:20:56,488 --> 00:20:58,624
Actually, what I want from you is,

330
00:20:58,890 --> 00:21:04,129
I want to know what will happen if
Goldberg's surgery is a success.

331
00:21:04,529 --> 00:21:08,000
Well, of course, Totei University Hospital
would make a lot of money.

332
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,270
That Nicholas Tange, you see,
he's not that simple.

333
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:15,874
His secret plan is to get
a huge investment from Goldberg Bank

334
00:21:16,308 --> 00:21:19,645
and milk us for everything we've got.
Darn him.

335
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:25,851
"Totei University Medical Resort
development plan"?

336
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:28,954
"Lake Mashu Satellite Hospital 39"?
That's where I was!

337
00:21:30,889 --> 00:21:33,959
That Tange is coming in here,
claiming that

338
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:37,129
he will reorganize the management,

339
00:21:37,229 --> 00:21:40,799
but he's breaking up
Totei University Hospital,

340
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:44,236
and selling it off piece by piece.
He's a vulture!

341
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:47,606
How dare he do this to Lake Mashu.
Darn him.

342
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:50,742
He's forgotten his debt to me
for inviting him here.

343
00:21:51,009 --> 00:21:53,245
Now that it's come to this,

344
00:21:53,412 --> 00:21:55,881
we have to strike before we're struck.

345
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,051
All right.

346
00:22:01,386 --> 00:22:02,988
I, Ebina Takashi,

347
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:07,159
will work like my life depends on this.
However,

348
00:22:08,026 --> 00:22:10,829
I'd like you to take care of
my family after I'm gone.

349
00:22:10,896 --> 00:22:14,399
Hold on a second here!
What I want from you is,

350
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:20,305
I want you to get dirt on him
and tell me about it.

351
00:22:20,405 --> 00:22:21,773
Oh, I see. That was a shock.

352
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,508
What's wrong with you?

353
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:26,578
ASAKUSA KANNON
ASAKUSA GOOD LUCK CHARM

354
00:22:43,428 --> 00:22:47,499
His father got a high fever
after an appendectomy

355
00:22:48,066 --> 00:22:49,534
and died.

356
00:22:51,103 --> 00:22:53,238
Yes? Who is it?

357
00:22:56,408 --> 00:23:00,278
Come in. Sorry about today.

358
00:23:00,445 --> 00:23:03,982
Five thousand yen for all three of them.
That's such a rip-off.

359
00:23:04,316 --> 00:23:07,285
I'd like to talk to Dr. Daimon.

360
00:23:07,352 --> 00:23:10,522
Go right ahead. It's rather messy, though.

361
00:23:10,622 --> 00:23:11,923
Okay. Go ahead.

362
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:14,926
- Have a seat.
- May I?

363
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:25,103
Seven insists on returning home
to get surgery.

364
00:23:25,837 --> 00:23:28,807
He's even decided on a surgeon in the US.

365
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:34,312
But I want you to do the surgery,
Dr. Daimon.

366
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:37,149
Oh, my! What a great offer.

367
00:23:37,716 --> 00:23:38,884
Why?

368
00:23:39,117 --> 00:23:41,553
Nobody can talk back to him.

369
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:46,992
In the US and in Japan,
everyone does what he tells them.

370
00:23:47,793 --> 00:23:51,763
But you told him exactly
how you felt, Dr. Daimon.

371
00:23:52,230 --> 00:23:54,900
For a patient on the brink of
life and death,

372
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:57,702
you said you would always save them.

373
00:23:58,970 --> 00:24:03,475
When you heard about Seven's father,
you said you wouldn't let him die.

374
00:24:04,676 --> 00:24:06,445
Dr. Daimon,

375
00:24:06,845 --> 00:24:10,148
please take care of Seven.

376
00:24:13,418 --> 00:24:15,353
But, I'm not kind.

377
00:24:21,159 --> 00:24:25,464
Natalie, how would you like to
have dinner with us?

378
00:24:25,530 --> 00:24:27,199
I made <i>kitsune</i> udon.

379
00:24:28,166 --> 00:24:29,468
I would love to.

380
00:24:30,602 --> 00:24:33,638
- I'm feeling a bit peckish.
- "Peckish"?

381
00:24:33,772 --> 00:24:36,608
Your Japanese is really great.

382
00:24:39,010 --> 00:24:40,712
- Hurry up.
- I am.

383
00:24:41,580 --> 00:24:43,648
<i>You've helped me, so I'm sorry about this.</i>

384
00:24:44,115 --> 00:24:47,586
Why are you quitting? You've got talent.

385
00:24:48,086 --> 00:24:49,287
I'm sorry.

386
00:24:49,754 --> 00:24:53,792
I have to get revenge for my boss.

387
00:24:54,025 --> 00:24:56,194
- Get revenge for your boss?
- Yes.

388
00:24:57,229 --> 00:25:00,165
- There are bad people like that?
- Yes, there are.

389
00:25:01,266 --> 00:25:04,636
When you look at him,
he doesn't look that bad.

390
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:06,605
See. Handsome guy, right?

391
00:25:06,738 --> 00:25:09,508
Hey! I know this guy.

392
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:11,209
You do?

393
00:25:11,309 --> 00:25:14,913
He's an acquaintance of
the boss of my boss.

394
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:17,716
I sometimes meet him at auctions.

395
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:19,951
- Auctions?
- Yes.

396
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:21,453
Look.

397
00:25:22,687 --> 00:25:24,923
You're right. Where is that?

398
00:25:24,990 --> 00:25:26,458
Bora Bora.

399
00:25:27,492 --> 00:25:29,327
"Bola"?

400
00:25:29,461 --> 00:25:30,729
Bora Bora!

401
00:25:30,996 --> 00:25:33,198
Since then, I haven't slept well.

402
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:36,968
I knew it. Me either.

403
00:25:38,303 --> 00:25:40,672
It's unclear if he has allergies too.

404
00:25:41,506 --> 00:25:43,341
Is it okay to operate?

405
00:25:43,942 --> 00:25:47,312
If something goes wrong
because we can't speak English--

406
00:25:47,479 --> 00:25:49,014
English is the least of your problems.

407
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:54,219
I'm not sure you're even fit
to be humans, let alone doctors.

408
00:25:57,022 --> 00:25:58,223
What did you just say?

409
00:25:58,323 --> 00:25:59,991
- Oh... I...
- Dr. Kaji!

410
00:26:00,525 --> 00:26:01,927
I'm sorry...

411
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:03,628
Thank you.

412
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:06,131
Well said.

413
00:26:07,198 --> 00:26:10,302
- We need to do the screening again.
- Right.

414
00:26:12,103 --> 00:26:14,205
You're doing it again? Good.

415
00:26:50,041 --> 00:26:54,713
What? You need a translator?
You should have asked me.

416
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:57,048
- I'll do it.
- Thank you.

417
00:26:57,949 --> 00:27:01,219
I'm sorry for shouting at you
in the conference. Thanks for this.

418
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:03,888
You don't need to apologize.

419
00:27:03,989 --> 00:27:06,424
The problem is
Japanese-English language education.

420
00:27:06,491 --> 00:27:09,527
After ten years of classes,
we still can't have a conversation.

421
00:27:12,797 --> 00:27:15,967
- What the heck did you say?
- Director Kaji!

422
00:27:16,234 --> 00:27:17,769
- Why did you say that?
- Calm down!

423
00:27:17,869 --> 00:27:19,704
I've had it!

424
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:29,080
What's the matter?

425
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:43,361
Seven?

426
00:27:47,399 --> 00:27:48,600
Seven!

427
00:27:49,034 --> 00:27:50,568
- Emergency stretcher!
- Right!

428
00:27:51,670 --> 00:27:54,205
- Keep your hands off him!
- This is no time for that!

429
00:27:54,272 --> 00:27:55,407
- Hurry!
- Right!

430
00:27:55,473 --> 00:27:57,942
Seven has vomited blood.
Prep a treatment room!

431
00:27:58,043 --> 00:27:58,943
Hurry!

432
00:28:03,248 --> 00:28:04,249
Mr. Goldberg!

433
00:28:04,315 --> 00:28:07,485
Sudden pain and vomiting blood.
Possible tumor tissue bleeding.

434
00:28:07,552 --> 00:28:09,320
He needs surgery right away.
Let me operate.

435
00:28:09,387 --> 00:28:12,257
No. I won't let you operate
without the patient's approval.

436
00:28:12,490 --> 00:28:16,795
Mr. Goldberg said he doesn't want
you operating on him, Dr. Daimon.

437
00:28:17,395 --> 00:28:20,432
If he sues, the damages will be
so immense, we can't pay for it.

438
00:28:20,799 --> 00:28:24,069
Please, Dr. Kaji,
give him the perfect surgery.

439
00:28:26,071 --> 00:28:27,172
Yes, sir.

440
00:28:29,107 --> 00:28:30,241
Let's go.

441
00:28:31,843 --> 00:28:34,512
- Dr. Daimon!
- Wait!

442
00:28:35,346 --> 00:28:37,649
Hey! Are you sure it's all right?

443
00:28:38,116 --> 00:28:39,684
Cut that out.

444
00:28:40,752 --> 00:28:45,056
OPERATING ROOM

445
00:28:48,927 --> 00:28:52,564
BP, 90 over 65. Pulse, 92.

446
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:55,033
We will now perform a total gastrectomy

447
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:57,368
via laparoscope on Seven Goldberg.

448
00:28:57,469 --> 00:28:59,070
Please begin, Dr. Kaji.

449
00:28:59,170 --> 00:29:01,039
- Let's hurry. Scalpel.
- Here.

450
00:29:09,247 --> 00:29:10,482
- Pean forceps.
- Here.

451
00:29:18,456 --> 00:29:19,657
- Trocar.
- Here.

452
00:29:25,630 --> 00:29:26,464
Here.

453
00:29:34,672 --> 00:29:36,574
I'll remove the accretion
from the greater omentum.

454
00:29:36,641 --> 00:29:38,610
First assistant, retract the intestine.

455
00:29:38,676 --> 00:29:39,611
Right.

456
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:42,747
EtCO2 is rising.

457
00:29:43,081 --> 00:29:45,083
- It's over 55.
- What?

458
00:29:48,052 --> 00:29:50,321
Increase ventilation rate and draw blood.

459
00:29:50,855 --> 00:29:52,257
This is bad.

460
00:29:55,493 --> 00:29:57,796
Pulse rising, 148.

461
00:29:58,496 --> 00:30:01,199
- What?
- BP falling, 85 over 50.

462
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,101
What happened?

463
00:30:04,102 --> 00:30:05,537
I don't know the cause.

464
00:30:05,703 --> 00:30:08,540
Could he be going into
anaphylactic shock from an allergy?

465
00:30:08,606 --> 00:30:12,377
His "yes" on allergies
in the screening was a "no"?

466
00:30:15,079 --> 00:30:18,449
I knew it! "Yes" meant he has allergies!

467
00:30:18,683 --> 00:30:20,852
Abdominal wall firmness, abnormal.

468
00:30:22,253 --> 00:30:24,155
- Give him rocuronium.
- Right.

469
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:25,824
- Get it now.
- Right.

470
00:30:27,559 --> 00:30:30,662
What's your problem?
I told you to give him a perfect surgery!

471
00:30:34,232 --> 00:30:37,202
Dr. Kaji was going to screen him again.

472
00:30:37,368 --> 00:30:39,537
But then he suddenly needed
emergency surgery.

473
00:30:40,271 --> 00:30:43,274
It's possible there was an error
during the screening.

474
00:30:43,641 --> 00:30:45,143
Are you serious?

475
00:30:48,279 --> 00:30:49,881
- Let's pull out for now.
- Right.

476
00:30:52,383 --> 00:30:53,952
- Rapid transfusion.
- Right.

477
00:30:54,819 --> 00:30:56,688
This could cause
peritoneal insufflation trouble.

478
00:30:56,821 --> 00:30:58,556
Blood gas results and rocuronium.

479
00:31:00,592 --> 00:31:03,261
It says he's undergoing acidosis.

480
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:04,863
Dr. Kaji.

481
00:31:04,963 --> 00:31:06,564
It's an allergy.

482
00:31:06,764 --> 00:31:08,299
- Intravenous adrenaline.
- Right.

483
00:31:08,366 --> 00:31:09,534
No!

484
00:31:10,835 --> 00:31:12,537
This isn't an allergy.

485
00:31:12,837 --> 00:31:14,839
- It's not an allergy?
- Dr. Daimon?

486
00:31:14,939 --> 00:31:17,041
- Then what is it?
- What's his temperature?

487
00:31:17,175 --> 00:31:18,843
It's over 42 degrees!

488
00:31:18,943 --> 00:31:22,814
I knew it. He's got a fever.
This is malignant hyperthermia.

489
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:26,317
Stop the inhalation anesthesia.
Only use intravenous anesthesia.

490
00:31:26,651 --> 00:31:28,553
- Prep a dantrolene infusion.
- Right.

491
00:31:28,686 --> 00:31:29,621
Drop his temperature!

492
00:31:29,687 --> 00:31:32,357
- Ice bags and cold saline.
- Right.

493
00:31:33,157 --> 00:31:35,159
- Give me a hand.
- Right.

494
00:31:35,526 --> 00:31:37,195
Malignant hyperthermia?

495
00:31:37,695 --> 00:31:39,731
It's the same as Seven's father.

496
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:43,234
Malignant hyperthermia can be
passed down genetically.

497
00:31:43,601 --> 00:31:45,336
What's going on here?

498
00:31:46,170 --> 00:31:48,172
My plan is finished.

499
00:31:50,508 --> 00:31:54,012
Once his vitals stabilize,
we're switching surgery procedures.

500
00:31:54,112 --> 00:31:57,315
- Pylorus preserving gastrectomy.
- We're continuing?

501
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,017
Of course.

502
00:31:59,784 --> 00:32:00,618
Here.

503
00:32:07,125 --> 00:32:08,893
Dantrolene ready.

504
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:11,796
Infuse him with 160 milliliters
over 15 minutes.

505
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:18,269
SURGERY TIME

506
00:32:22,974 --> 00:32:25,777
His temperature has fallen
to 37.4 degrees.

507
00:32:25,877 --> 00:32:29,280
- Vitals?
- BP, 124 over 81.

508
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:32,116
Pulse, 78, sinus.

509
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:34,953
- Good. Let's open him up. Scalpel.
- Here.

510
00:32:35,887 --> 00:32:37,188
Dr. Daimon!

511
00:32:38,122 --> 00:32:39,657
Please!

512
00:32:40,658 --> 00:32:42,260
Save Seven!

513
00:32:45,997 --> 00:32:48,700
I never fail.

514
00:32:52,904 --> 00:32:54,372
I'll be first assistant.

515
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:01,145
Here.

516
00:33:04,082 --> 00:33:06,417
ASAKUSA KANNON

517
00:33:28,473 --> 00:33:30,575
Stomach excision complete.
Reconstructing now.

518
00:33:30,641 --> 00:33:32,043
- Stomach forceps.
- Here.

519
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:46,557
- What's his temperature?
- It's 36 degrees.

520
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:49,327
- Vitals stable.
- Done.

521
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:52,363
Watch his kidney functions post-op.

522
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:54,565
- Daimon.
- Dr. Daimon.

523
00:34:13,851 --> 00:34:16,287
The perfect surgery

524
00:34:18,122 --> 00:34:20,691
requires the perfect surgeon.

525
00:34:22,693 --> 00:34:23,694
Daimon!

526
00:34:27,098 --> 00:34:28,433
Daimon.

527
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:31,969
I'm sorry. I owe you one.

528
00:34:32,103 --> 00:34:35,006
We couldn't admit
that we can't speak English.

529
00:34:35,640 --> 00:34:37,675
We should have brought in a translator

530
00:34:38,009 --> 00:34:40,311
to check for any genetic abnormalities.

531
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,981
We're too proud,
so we didn't want to be disgraced.

532
00:34:44,682 --> 00:34:46,083
We regret what we did!

533
00:34:47,418 --> 00:34:49,420
You must be kidding me.

534
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:52,657
Pride?

535
00:34:53,524 --> 00:34:54,725
Disgrace?

536
00:34:55,726 --> 00:34:57,361
What total jerks!

537
00:34:58,563 --> 00:35:02,433
You could have killed that patient
for such trivial garbage as that!

538
00:35:06,204 --> 00:35:08,272
Don't operate on a patient like that.

539
00:35:24,489 --> 00:35:26,524
This feels so nice!

540
00:35:30,895 --> 00:35:33,364
Who would have thought this day
would come for a plebe like me?

541
00:35:33,431 --> 00:35:34,532
It's such an honor.

542
00:35:35,433 --> 00:35:37,602
Quit calling yourself a plebe.

543
00:35:37,768 --> 00:35:39,704
- We're going to have a filet.
- Thank you.

544
00:35:40,938 --> 00:35:42,874
More importantly, Ebina,

545
00:35:43,007 --> 00:35:45,076
what's that information you got?

546
00:35:45,376 --> 00:35:48,012
Can you show it to me?

547
00:35:50,448 --> 00:35:52,216
- Here it is.
- What?

548
00:35:58,856 --> 00:36:00,291
Have I been of help?

549
00:36:02,860 --> 00:36:05,496
- Just drink your wine.
- Thank you.

550
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:15,773
- That's delicious.
- Ebina.

551
00:36:17,275 --> 00:36:18,676
- This, you see,
- Yes?

552
00:36:19,610 --> 00:36:24,582
without a doubt,
this is proof that Tange used info about

553
00:36:24,782 --> 00:36:28,486
Totei University Hospital VIP patients
for insider trading.

554
00:36:28,553 --> 00:36:32,890
Right. Tange obtained huge sums
of money this way

555
00:36:32,957 --> 00:36:35,159
and bought a deserted island in Bora Bora.

556
00:36:35,326 --> 00:36:37,695
I have photos from Bora Bora
that prove it.

557
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:39,697
Here.

558
00:36:40,164 --> 00:36:44,001
Oh, you're right.
Where in the world did you get this stuff?

559
00:36:44,101 --> 00:36:45,970
From my boss at my part-time job.

560
00:36:46,037 --> 00:36:47,939
That one you wore white makeup for?

561
00:36:48,005 --> 00:36:49,974
- Right.
- Really?

562
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:52,643
Oh, by the way.

563
00:36:52,843 --> 00:36:54,679
These are foreign remittances.

564
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:56,614
- You heard of cryptocurrency?
- Yes.

565
00:36:56,681 --> 00:36:58,849
That's how he made his purchases.

566
00:36:58,916 --> 00:37:00,918
Apparently, that's hard to trace.

567
00:37:01,018 --> 00:37:02,687
I don't really understand it, though.

568
00:37:04,622 --> 00:37:05,957
- Ebina.
- Yes?

569
00:37:06,591 --> 00:37:09,760
- Well done, my friend!
- Thanks.

570
00:37:10,127 --> 00:37:14,765
To me, you are my one and only

571
00:37:15,299 --> 00:37:17,235
very precious subordinate.

572
00:37:17,635 --> 00:37:18,703
Thank you.

573
00:37:18,803 --> 00:37:23,407
From now on,
look forward to your advancement.

574
00:37:23,541 --> 00:37:26,477
- Really?
- Yes. You'll climb like crazy.

575
00:37:26,677 --> 00:37:27,979
Thank you so much.

576
00:37:38,656 --> 00:37:39,824
Assistant Director,

577
00:37:40,558 --> 00:37:43,461
that 500-million-dollar loan
from Goldberg Bank,

578
00:37:43,894 --> 00:37:45,563
it looks like we're going to get it.

579
00:37:45,630 --> 00:37:46,897
MEDICAL RESORT PLAN FINANCING

580
00:37:47,231 --> 00:37:48,633
Is that right?

581
00:37:49,033 --> 00:37:53,037
With this, the medical resort
that you've conceptualized

582
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:55,172
will become a reality.

583
00:37:56,040 --> 00:37:57,308
Samejima.

584
00:37:58,776 --> 00:38:00,211
Well done.

585
00:38:01,178 --> 00:38:02,513
Nicholas.

586
00:38:03,381 --> 00:38:05,416
I've never felt better!

587
00:38:06,684 --> 00:38:08,152
Samejima.

588
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:11,355
I want to listen to that.
It's been a while.

589
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:13,224
Right.

590
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:25,202
Five-hundred-million-dollar samba!

591
00:38:25,803 --> 00:38:27,238
Amore!

592
00:38:27,972 --> 00:38:30,408
Five hundred million, Samejima!

593
00:38:30,841 --> 00:38:32,810
- Loosen up!
- Nicholas!

594
00:38:38,282 --> 00:38:39,984
Please, continue.

595
00:38:40,351 --> 00:38:42,887
Something good must have happened.

596
00:38:43,688 --> 00:38:45,256
I'm so glad to hear it.

597
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:49,160
Once again,
I'm from Kanbara Famous Doctor Agency.

598
00:38:49,527 --> 00:38:51,762
Thank you for using Michiko Daimon

599
00:38:51,929 --> 00:38:56,367
during the emergency
of Mr. Goldberg's surgery.

600
00:38:57,001 --> 00:38:59,036
As we always do,

601
00:38:59,203 --> 00:39:03,274
we'll allow Director Kaji
and Totei University Hospital

602
00:39:03,474 --> 00:39:06,577
to take all the credit for it.

603
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:09,313
This is a melon.

604
00:39:12,516 --> 00:39:14,251
This is the bill.

605
00:39:17,121 --> 00:39:20,458
Samejima, pay this.

606
00:39:21,459 --> 00:39:23,094
You won't even look at the price?

607
00:39:23,394 --> 00:39:25,396
Thank you.

608
00:39:25,596 --> 00:39:29,767
I hope you continue to use Michiko Daimon.

609
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:32,536
- Thank you too.
- Goodbye.

610
00:39:45,449 --> 00:39:48,753
Thank you, Nichotan!

611
00:39:50,855 --> 00:39:57,194
Nichotan...

612
00:40:01,966 --> 00:40:03,968
Keep on eating.

613
00:40:04,135 --> 00:40:06,604
- That's great!
- More will be ready soon.

614
00:40:08,472 --> 00:40:12,042
Dr. Daimon, thank you for saving Seven.

615
00:40:12,777 --> 00:40:14,512
Since I didn't take out your whole stomach

616
00:40:14,612 --> 00:40:16,847
and left half, it's good, isn't it?

617
00:40:18,182 --> 00:40:20,885
Thanks for the surgery,
and for giving him so much hair too.

618
00:40:21,051 --> 00:40:23,454
You did that? Amazing.

619
00:40:24,021 --> 00:40:27,191
I've changed my opinion about
Japanese doctors.

620
00:40:27,491 --> 00:40:29,994
B-rank cuisine is awesome too.

621
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:31,262
Isn't it?

622
00:40:41,572 --> 00:40:43,841
Michiko, go ahead and go.

623
00:40:43,941 --> 00:40:45,176
Not right now.

624
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:51,048
- Seriously?
- Yes.

625
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:55,686
- But I still won't.
- Michiko, what's wrong with you?

626
00:40:57,855 --> 00:40:59,523
There's a patient I want to operate on.

627
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:03,527
Delicious!

628
00:41:03,727 --> 00:41:05,362
Here, have some <i>takoyaki.</i>

629
00:41:05,563 --> 00:41:07,298
Go right ahead.

630
00:41:12,937 --> 00:41:16,674
We got the 500 million for
the Bora Bora facility!

631
00:41:16,841 --> 00:41:19,243
I've never felt better!

632
00:41:19,343 --> 00:41:21,579
Me too, Nicholas.

633
00:41:21,912 --> 00:41:24,582
Samejima! Loosen up!

634
00:41:31,355 --> 00:41:33,023
Tokyo Public Prosecutor
investigative team.

635
00:41:33,457 --> 00:41:35,125
You're Nicholas Tange, right?

636
00:41:36,594 --> 00:41:37,695
You're under arrest

637
00:41:37,795 --> 00:41:41,365
for violation of the Financial Instruments
and Exchange Act.

638
00:41:41,532 --> 00:41:43,200
ARREST WARRANT

639
00:41:44,034 --> 00:41:45,402
I'll handle this.

640
00:41:46,537 --> 00:41:47,738
Hurry!

641
00:41:56,714 --> 00:41:58,182
Hold on here!

642
00:42:11,262 --> 00:42:14,632
Wait. That's a Stradivarius.

643
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:16,734
It's worth 800 million.

644
00:42:25,643 --> 00:42:27,211
What are you doing with your mouth?

645
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:40,157
What is this? This is ridiculous!
Darn that mouth of yours!

646
00:42:40,324 --> 00:42:42,226
What's with this? This is crazy!

647
00:42:47,031 --> 00:42:48,198
No, you should say "no."

648
00:42:48,299 --> 00:42:49,199
Why?

649
00:42:51,769 --> 00:42:52,870
Quit messing up.

650
00:42:55,639 --> 00:42:57,675
What did you just say? What did she say?

651
00:42:57,841 --> 00:42:59,577
What's with this? I've had it!

652
00:42:59,643 --> 00:43:03,414
I'll only ever operate on
Japanese patients!

653
00:43:03,814 --> 00:43:05,416
I can't stand your mouth!

654
00:43:06,216 --> 00:43:08,085
I can't stand this humiliation any longer!

655
00:43:08,152 --> 00:43:09,753
Quit crying! Pull yourself together!

656
00:43:09,853 --> 00:43:12,122
Weak fish will be eaten by the black bass.

657
00:43:12,323 --> 00:43:13,791
Shut up!

658
00:43:15,092 --> 00:43:19,496
<i>This woman hates groups,
hates authority, and hates restrictions.</i>

659
00:43:20,364 --> 00:43:23,834
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

660
00:43:23,968 --> 00:43:25,703
<i>are her weapons.</i>

661
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:28,839
I did it to protect
this Totei University Hospital!

662
00:43:29,006 --> 00:43:31,075
Assistant Director Tange is innocent!

663
00:43:31,842 --> 00:43:35,679
This hospital deep in the red,
I brought it back from the dead!

664
00:43:36,080 --> 00:43:39,183
At this rate, foreigners will
buy it all up at bargain prices!

665
00:43:42,486 --> 00:43:46,724
Japan's assets
and magnificent technology...

666
00:43:48,359 --> 00:43:50,361
We Japanese shouldn't be
trying to destroy them!

667
00:43:51,395 --> 00:43:55,966
If you do this, all the weak
Japanese fish will be gobbled up!

668
00:43:56,934 --> 00:43:59,003
How come you can't understand that?

669
00:44:05,576 --> 00:44:08,012
The black bass was arrested.

670
00:44:15,819 --> 00:44:17,554
Dr. Daimon.

671
00:44:19,857 --> 00:44:21,692
You understand, don't you?

672
00:44:21,925 --> 00:44:23,160
We can't allow

673
00:44:23,260 --> 00:44:26,997
invasive species to throw
their weight around anymore.

674
00:44:28,699 --> 00:44:31,201
This, you see, Dr. Daimon,

675
00:44:31,902 --> 00:44:35,773
happened by my hand.

676
00:44:38,642 --> 00:44:41,311
Thank you for your hard work.

677
00:44:42,713 --> 00:44:48,452
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,
otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

678
00:44:49,353 --> 00:44:51,689
I know a spell for never failing.

679
00:44:51,755 --> 00:44:53,223
<i>She's a former Miss Totei University.</i>

680
00:44:53,290 --> 00:44:56,360
<i>That means she's so good that even
world-famous doctors recognize her.</i>

681
00:44:56,460 --> 00:44:58,896
My life belongs to the citizens.

682
00:44:59,063 --> 00:45:01,498
- I'll do it.
<i>- Will you be my assistant?</i>

683
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:03,767
That's not what a doctor is.
